---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import { site } from "../site.config.mjs";
import { u } from "../lib/atlas.js";
---
<Base title="About" description="What this site is, what it quotes and does not, and how discussion works.">
  <div class="wrap" style="max-width:var(--measure);padding-top:34px">
    <h1>About</h1>
    <p class="dek">A reading companion to the Theravāda Abhidhamma, made as a study aid and not as an authority.</p>
    <h2>What it follows</h2>
    <p>The order and the numbers follow Bhikkhu Bodhi's <i>A Comprehensive Manual of Abhidhamma</i>. The site retells and cites the <i>Manual</i>; it does not reproduce its text or tables, which belong to the Buddhist Publication Society. References like "IV §6" are to its chapters and sections, so you can read the source alongside.</p>
    <p>Suttas are cited by their SuttaCentral numbers. Short sutta passages are retold, or quoted from Bhikkhu Sujato's translations, which he has placed in the public domain.</p>
    <h2>What is commentarial</h2>
    <p>Much of the Abhidhamma's system, such as the seventeen-moment process or the count of thirty-one planes, comes from the commentaries rather than the canonical books. Each concept page says so in "In the texts". Readings of stories are marked as study aids.</p>
    <h2 id="discussion">Reflect and discuss</h2>
    <p>Each concept and reading ends with an opening question. Under it is a box for your own answer: write before you read the model answer. Your reflections are private. They are kept in your browser, and, if you sign in, in your account too, so they follow you between devices. <a href={u("reflections/")}>My reflections</a> collects them and lets you download them.</p>
    <p>Below that is the page's discussion. Anyone can read it. To write, <a href={u("account/")}>sign in</a> with Google, GitHub or an email address. You can edit or delete your own comments at any time.</p>
    <h2 id="privacy">Privacy</h2>
    <p>The site keeps only what you give it: your name, the email you sign in with, your comments (public) and your reflections (private to you). It uses no analytics and no advertising. Deleting your account from <a href={u("account/")}>your account page</a> deletes your profile, comments and synced reflections. Reflections kept only in your browser never leave it.</p>
    <h2 id="licence">Licence</h2>
    <p>The text, drawings and data on this site are licensed under <a href="https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/" rel="license">Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0</a>. You may share and adapt them for any purpose, with credit to <i>Abhidhamma: a reading companion</i> and a link back. Anything you make from them must carry the same licence. The code is MIT. Bodhi's <i>Manual</i> and other people's translations keep their own terms; see <code>LICENSE.md</code> in the source.</p>
    <h2>Corrections</h2>
    <p>Every page can be wrong. To point out an error or suggest a source, open an issue or a pull request at <a href={site.repo}>the source</a>.</p>
  </div>
</Base>
